sp;<strong>21 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>40 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per UPPSC Medical Officer, Other Posts Recruitment Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>UPPSC Medical Officer, Other Posts</strong></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>2026 : Vacancy Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Total Posts : 2158 Posts</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>No. of Posts</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"> Medical Officer, Community Health</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">884</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Veterinary Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">404</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Swasthya Shiksha Adhikari</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">221</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Homoeopathic Medical Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">265</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Inspector of Drugs</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">26</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Dental Surgeon</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">157</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Chikitsa Adhikari (Ayurveda)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">168</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Chikitsa Adhikari (Unani)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">25</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Chikitsa Adhikari (Homoeopathic)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">07</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Vetting Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">01</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>UPPSC Medical Officer, Other Posts Recruitment 2026 : Educational Qualification</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Medical Officer, Community Health</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Degree in Ayurveda or Unani Tib of a University established by law in India or a qualification recognised by the Government as equivalent thereto.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Registration as a Vaidya or a Hakeem with the Board of Indian Medicine, Uttar Pradesh</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">At least six month’s Professional experience in State Ayurvedic, Unani or AllopathicHospital or dispensary.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Veterinary Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">A degree of Bachelor of Veterinary Science and Animal Husbandry (B.V.Sc. &amp; A.H.) from a University established by law in India or a degree recognised by the Government.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Swasthya Shiksha Adhikari</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">A candidate for direct recruitment must possess a Master’s Degree from a recognised University in Sociology or any subject of Social Science. </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Homoeopathic Medical Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">A recognised degree in Homoeopathy, the duration of study of which is not less than five years according to its syllabus or course</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Inspector of Drugs</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Degree in Pharmacy or Pharmaceutical Sciences or Medicine with specialization in Clinical Pharmacology or Microbiology or equivalent from a recognized University</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Dental Surgeon</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">A candidate for direct recruitment to the Service must possess at least B.D.S. (Bachelor of Dental Surgery) degree from a recognised university or an equivalent qualification recognised by the Indian Dental Council.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Chikitsa Adhikari (Ayurveda)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">A degree in Ayurveda of a University established by law in India or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Five years degree or diploma in Ayurvedic of the Board of Indian Medicine, Uttar Pradesh.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Registration as a Vaidya with the Board of Indian Medicine, Uttar Pradesh and</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Atleast six months Professional experience of State Ayurvedic or Allopathic Hospital or dispensary.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Chikitsa Adhikari (Unani)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"> A degree in Unani Tib of a University established by law in India. or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Five years degree or diploma in Unani Tib of the Board of Indian Medicine, Uttar Pradesh.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Registration as a Hakeem with the Board of Indian Medicine, Uttar Pradesh and</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">At least six months Professional experience of State Unani or Allopathic Hospital or dispensary.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Chikitsa Adhikari (Homoeopathic)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">A recognised degree in Homoeopathy, the duration of study of which is not less than five years according to its syllabus or course or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Arecognised Diploma in Homoeopathy, the duration of study of which is not less than four years according to its syllabus or course Provided that preference will be given to degree holders.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">The applicant should be duly registered with the Homoeopathic Medicine Board, Uttar Pradesh.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Vetting Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Bachelor of Arts degree (with English Literature or Hindi Literature as one of the subjects) or Bachelor of Science degree or Bachelor of Commerce degree with a minimum 50% marks from a University established by law in India or a qualification recognised by the Government as equivalent thereto, and, three years Bachelor of Laws degree with a minimum fifty percent marks from a University established by law in India.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Download UPPSC Veterinary Officer Exam Date 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">In order to download their UPPSC Veterinary Officer Exam Date candidates are required to go to the important link section provided below.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After getting the link candidates need to click it for downloading their UPPSC Veterinary Officer Exam Date.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates need to provide their following details-:</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Registration No. /Roll No.</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>DOB/Password</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Captcha Code(if specified)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After providing their details appropriately candidates will be able to check their UPPSC Veterinary Officer Exam Date.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates can also check their UPPSC Veterinary Officer Exam Date from official site of the UPPSC.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><